[groq-gpt-oss] evals/prompts/lib/skill-p:
**Short answer**

*Use a **`color-relief`** layer.*  
The `color-relief` layer type is the only way to colour a `raster-dem` source on the fly.  
Inside its `paint` object you set **`color-relief-color`** to an `interpolate` expression that reads the special `["elevation"]` expression (meters above the DEM’s datum). The expression builds the hypsometric ramp you want (blue → green → brown → white).

Below is a complete, ready-to-copy example that shows:

1. Adding the DEM source (`type: "raster-dem"`).  
2. Adding a `color-relief` layer that tints the terrain.  
3. Tweaking opacity and exaggeration if you also have 3-D terrain turned on.

---

## 1. Add the DEM source (once)

```js
// MapLibre GL JS ≥ v5.6
map.addSource('terrain-dem', {
  type: 'raster-dem',
  // URL can be a TileJSON, a template string, or a PMTiles URL, etc.
  url: 'https://my.tileserver.com/terrain/{z}/{x}/{y}.webp',
  // optional, but recommended – tells the decoder how the DEM is encoded
  // (e.g. "terrarium", "mapbox", "raw")
  // encoding: 'terrarium',
  maxzoom: 14
});
```

> **Note** – The source is *only* a DEM. If you also want a 3-D mesh you’ll later call `map.setTerrain({source: 'terrain-dem'})`. The `color-relief` layer works **without** `setTerrain`; it just paints the DEM as a raster image.

---

## 2. Add the hypsometric (color-relief) layer

```js
map.addLayer({
  id: 'hypsometric-tint',
  type: 'color-relief',          // ← the layer type you asked for
  source: 'terrain-dem',
  // No "source-layer" – raster-dem sources have no vector layers
  paint: {
    // The colour ramp – change the stops to suit your palette
    'color-relief-color': [
      'interpolate',
      ['linear'],
      ['elevation'],               // <-- special expression, only works here
      // ---- elevation (m) ----   ---- colour ----
      -10,   '#2e3f5a',   // deep water (a dark blue)
       0,    '#2c7bb6',   // sea level – bright blue
     200,    '#61a6d1',   // shallow water / low coast
     500,    '#a6d96a',   // lowlands – green
    1500,    '#ffffbf',   // mid-elevation – light yellow
    2500,    '#fdae61',   // sub-alpine – orange-brown
    3500,    '#d73027',   // alpine – red-brown
    4500,    '#ffffff'    // snow-capped peaks – white
    ],

    // Optional – make the tint semi-transparent so you can still see a base map
    'color-relief-opacity': 0.85,

    // Optional – if you have a 3-D terrain mesh you can soften the colour
    // by resampling (GL JS 5.20+).  "linear" is the default.
    // 'resampling': 'linear'
  }
});
```

### How the ramp works

| Elevation (m) | Colour (hex) | Visual meaning |
|---------------|--------------|----------------|
| **-10**       | `#2e3f5a`    | Deep ocean (dark blue) |
| **0**         | `#2c7bb6`    | Sea level – bright blue |
| **200**       | `#61a6d1`    | Shallow water / low coast |
| **500**       | `#a6d96a`    | Lowland vegetation – green |
| **1500**      | `#ffffbf`    | Mid-elevation – light yellow |
| **2500**      | `#fdae61`    | Sub-alpine – orange-brown |
| **3500**      | `#d73027`    | Alpine rock – red-brown |
| **4500**      | `#ffffff`    | Snow-capped peaks – white |

*Feel free to add, remove, or move stops. The `interpolate` expression will smoothly blend between them.*

---

## 3. (Optional) Show the same DEM as 3-D terrain

If you also want a true 3-D surface you can enable it **after** the `color-relief` layer is added:

```js
// Turn the DEM into a mesh that the map can fly over
map.setTerrain({
  source: 'terrain-dem',
  exaggeration: 1.2   // tweak to make relief more dramatic
});

// Give the user a sky so the horizon isn’t just the page background
map.setSky({
  'sky-color': '#199EF3',
  'sky-horizon-blend': 0.5,
  'horizon-color': '#ffffff',
  'fog-color': '#cceeff',
  'fog-ground-blend': 0.3
});
```

> **Important** – The `color-relief` layer works **independently** of `setTerrain`.  
> If you turn terrain off (`map.setTerrain(null)`), the hypsometric tint stays visible because it is just a raster rendering of the DEM.

---

## 4. Full minimal example (HTML + JS)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre – Hypsometric Tint</title>
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@5.6.0/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@5.6.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    body, html { margin:0; padding:0; height:100%; }
    #map { width:100%; height:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>
<script>
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: {
      version: 8,
      sources: {},          // we’ll add sources programmatically
      layers: []            // same for layers
    },
    center: [12.4924, 41.8902], // Rome (just an example)
    zoom: 6,
    pitch: 45,               // tilt so you can see the 3-D mesh (optional)
    bearing: 0
  });

  map.on('load', () => {
    // 1️⃣ DEM source
    map.addSource('terrain-dem', {
      type: 'raster-dem',
      url: 'https://tiles.example.com/terrain/{z}/{x}/{y}.webp',
      maxzoom: 14
    });

    // 2️⃣ Hypsometric tint
    map.addLayer({
      id: 'hypsometric-tint',
      type: 'color-relief',
      source: 'terrain-dem',
      paint: {
        'color-relief-color': [
          'interpolate',
          ['linear'],
          ['elevation'],
          -10, '#2e3f5a',
           0,  '#2c7bb6',
         200,  '#61a6d1',
         500,  '#a6d96a',
        1500,  '#ffffbf',
        2500,  '#fdae61',
        3500,  '#d73027',
        4500,  '#ffffff'
        ],
        'color-relief-opacity': 0.85
      }
    });

    // 3️⃣ (optional) 3-D terrain + sky
    map.setTerrain({ source: 'terrain-dem', exaggeration: 1.2 });
    map.setSky({
      'sky-color': '#199EF3',
      'sky-horizon-blend': 0.5,
      'horizon-color': '#ffffff',
      'fog-color': '#cceeff',
      'fog-ground-blend': 0.3
    });
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

